@auth.sigil from Auth import { renter }
@resource-management.sigil from ResourceManagement import {
    Room,
    base availability rules,
    requested time range,
}
@booking.sigil from Booking import { confirmed booking }

component BookingCalendarView {
    goal {
        Helps a renter understand room availability and confirmed booking records
        in the *room calendar* for a selected date range.

        Keeps calendar presentation and interaction separate from
        base availability rules and booking policies.
    }

    interface {
        The room calendar shows date navigation above a calendar of Rooms and
        confirmed bookings for a *selected date range*.

        The renter can move to the previous or next selected date range.

        The renter can select an available Room and requested time range to begin
        a booking request.

        The room calendar shows clear feedback while its data is loading or cannot
        be loaded.

        The room calendar uses this representative layout:
        ```text
        +------------------------------------------------------+
        | Previous | July 2026                      | Next     |
        +------------------------------------------------------+
        | Room     | 09:00 | 10:00 | 11:00 | 12:00            |
        +------------------------------------------------------+
        | Cedar    | Open  | Booked| Booked| Open              |
        | Maple    | Open  | Open  | Open  | Booked            |
        +------------------------------------------------------+
        ```

        Visual reference for the room calendar:
        ![Booking calendar layout](./booking-calendar-view.svg)

        The image provides layout guidance while the written room calendar
        interface defines required behavior.
    }

    state {
        The room calendar is loading while its data is requested.

        The room calendar is empty when no Rooms are available in the selected date
        range.

        The ready room calendar shows Rooms and confirmed bookings for the selected
        date range.

        The room calendar is failed when its data cannot be loaded.
    }

    logic {
        Previous and Next controls request the adjacent selected date range.

        Selecting an available Room and requested time range begins a booking request.

        Selecting a confirmed booking does not begin a booking request.

        Loading, empty, ready, and failed states replace the room calendar body
        without removing date navigation.
    }

    constraints {
        BookingCalendarView owns presentation and interaction for the room calendar,
        not Room availability or booking policy.

        The room calendar reads its data from the Calendar Read Model described by
        Slotted.

        The room calendar adapts to narrow screens without hiding date navigation
        or booking status.

        Each *calendar control* is reachable and operable with a keyboard.

        The room calendar communicates availability and confirmed booking status
        with text rather than color alone.
    }

    cases {
        A renter moves the calendar control to the next selected date range and sees
        its Rooms and confirmed bookings.

        A renter selects an open slot in a Room and begins a booking request.

        A renter cannot begin a booking request from a confirmed booking slot.

        The room calendar shows an empty message when the selected date range
        contains no available Rooms.

        The room calendar lets the renter retry after its data fails to load.
    }
}
